  "confounders": [
    "GEOLOCATION PROMPT PENDING (stated confounder). squallar-location's gate asks at startup on a fresh origin: LocationMemo defaults to enabled=true, attempts=0, the permission reads Prompt, so LocationGate::step calls request_location -> watchPosition (squallar-location/src/gate.rs, web.rs). Every driven Safari-tab leg is a fresh origin, so the iOS location prompt was raised; the user saw it and could not answer it while automation held the phone. No fix and no refusal reached the app. Evidence it did not stall this leg is in `leg_liveness` below. A rig-side seed avoids the request with no product change: localStorage squallar.location = {\"attempts\":2,\"enabled\":true} (may_ask() is then false); it was NOT used for this row.",
    "The Mac's Safari had Develop > iPhone > 'Connect via Network' enabled by the user before these legs; the WebDriver session added an Indirect (network) Web Inspector connection beside the Direct (USB) one.",
    "safari:deviceUDID was the HARDWARE udid 00008110-001108891192801E; the CoreDevice identifier 64A825AA-AE5A-510E-88B0-E29F52F57C1D is discarded by safaridriver as a UDID mismatch.",
    "Calibrate localStorage route: unreadable on this arm. Each calibrate run ended by the page's death, which terminates the automation session, and a second automation session starts on empty website data (probed 2026-09-13: session A wrote a key, session B on the same origin read 0 keys). Every calibrate figure here is the /rig/report route.",
    "Served build: app b92a784f7 (wasm sha256 in provenance); rig at the `commit` column.",
    "First WALL4 attempt (2026-09-13T01:46:31Z) lost its automation tab 1.5 s after the session connected (Mac log: 'Removed Drivable ... remote session was terminated'), before any tick; no alert or permission event was logged on the Mac. Its cause is not established. This row is the rerun at 01:51:41Z."
  ],
